---
title: Vegan Chili
portions: 6
category: Chili
source: "https://www.lovingitvegan.com/vegan-chili/"
---

## Vegetables

[Sweat] Heat the @olive-oil{30 ml} in a large #pot{} over medium heat. Sauté the @onion{150 g}(chopped), the @celery{100 g}(sliced) and the @carrot{120 g}(sliced) until softened, ~{10 min}.

[Bloom] Add the @garlic{12 g}(crushed), the @chili-powder{15 g}, the @cumin{2 g}, the @oregano{1 g}, the @cayenne-pepper{0.5 g} and the @smoked-paprika{2 g}. Cook until fragrant, ~{2 min}.

## Simmer

[Simmer] Add the @canned-tomatoes{784 g}, the @vegetable-stock{240 ml}, the @tomato-paste{60 g}, the @kidney-beans{260 g} and the @black-beans{260 g}. Stir and bring to a gentle simmer.

[Braise] Reduce the heat and simmer uncovered until the vegetables are cooked and the flavors have blended, ~{30 min}. Stir occasionally.

[Season] Stir in the @brown-sugar{25 g}. Season with @salt{} to taste.

## Serve

[Serve] Serve topped with diced @avocado{} and fresh @cilantro{}.
